---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Privacy Policy | Handed the Keys"
			description="Privacy policy for Handed the Keys."
		/>

		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
			}

			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
			}

			h2 {
				margin-top: 2.5rem;
			}

			.updated {
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
			}
		</style>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />

		<main>
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

			<p class="updated">Last updated: August 8, 2026</p>

			<p>
				Handed the Keys is a personal blog. The site is designed to collect as little
				personal information from visitors as reasonably possible.
			</p>

			<h2>Information collected</h2>

			<p>
				Handed the Keys does not currently require visitors to create an account,
				subscribe to a mailing list, or provide personal information in order to read
				the site.
			</p>

			<p>
				The site does not currently use advertising or analytics services that
				intentionally collect visitor information. This policy will be updated before
				such services are enabled.
			</p>

<h2>Names and identifying details</h2>

<p>
	Posts on Handed the Keys may describe real people and events. To protect
	privacy, names and other identifying details may be changed, particularly
	when a post involves students or other minors.
</p>
<p>
	When a pseudonym is used, Handed the Keys generally uses a Biblical	name. These pseudonyms are chosen only to distinguish people within a story
	and are not intended to suggest the person's real name, identity, or
	religious affiliation.
</p>

						<h2>Comments</h2>

			<p>
				Comments on individual blog posts are provided through Giscus, a commenting
				system powered by GitHub Discussions. Reading the blog does not require a
				GitHub account.
			</p>
			<p>
				Visitors who choose to comment or react must sign in with GitHub and authorize
				Giscus. Comments and reactions are stored in the public GitHub Discussions
				associated with Handed the Keys and may be publicly visible along with
				information from the visitor's GitHub profile.
			</p>
			<p>
				Giscus states that it does not track visitors or serve advertising. GitHub
				and Giscus may process information necessary to provide the commenting
				service according to their respective practices.
			</p>

			<h2>External links</h2>

			<p>
				Posts may contain links to other websites. Handed the Keys is not responsible
				for the privacy practices or content of external websites.
			</p>

			<h2>Future services</h2>

			<p>
				Handed the Keys may later use services such as website analytics or
				advertising. If those services are added, this policy will be updated to
				explain what information they collect and how that information is used.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

			<p>
				This Privacy Policy may be updated as the site develops or new features are
				added. The date at the top of this page will reflect the most recent revision.
			</p>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>